1
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:07,180
(Sea Talk)

2
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:10,840
I'll write it down then.

3
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:11,680
Okay.

4
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,520
Here it comes!

5
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:28,760
Okay.

6
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:36,160
There's a ceremony.

7
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:37,640
It even lights up.

8
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:39,240
Wow.

9
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:39,880
Would you join me

10
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:40,800
for Sea Talk?

11
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:53,610
Sure.

12
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:56,400
Sea Talk begins.

13
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,200
Okay.

14
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,180
(Sea Talk starts)

15
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:05,480
This one really startles you.

16
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:08,000
This one keeps surprising you.

17
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,440
This seashell is pretty nice.

18
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,880
It's quite shiny too.

19
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:18,720
Slow down.

20
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:27,480
Chen Hewen.

21
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:35,460
(Turns around)

22
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:37,120
What's wrong?

23
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,240
Nothing. I just feel bored.

24
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:42,440
Oh no. His heart's all over the place.

25
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,800
Being in this situation,

26
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:45,520
I feel like I'm really conflicted.

27
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:47,840
It's just...

28
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,440
There isn't much time left.

29
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,520
I don't want to leave with regrets.

30
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:56,320
Oh my gosh.

31
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,440
Chen Hewen, keep going!

32
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:09,560
Those looking for love need to hurry.

33
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:17,580
(Peeks out)

34
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,200
Liang Xiaoyu is here.

35
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:29,260
(Sighs)

36
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:39,180
(Softly)

37
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:51,460
(Carefully leaves)

38
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,880
She doesn't want to disturb him.

39
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:08,560
Who is it?

40
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:18,880
He didn't see her.

41
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:53,340
Oh my gosh.

42
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:00,120
That's amazing.

43
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:02,360
A second ago,

44
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:03,440
we were still in Hebei.

45
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,640
Really, I feel like...

46
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:08,080
Do you believe in free will?

47
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:11,200
Do you think you have free will?

48
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,920
I think I do.

49
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,160
I think I do too,

50
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:14,760
but...

51
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:17,720
right now I kind of believe in...

52
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,960
this feeling of fate.

53
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:25,120
Because so many things
feel too coincidental.

54
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,440
Like what?

55
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:28,300
For example, me coming here.

56
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:29,980
(Me coming here)

57
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:34,520
And everything
that happened after I came here.

58
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,840
So I kind of

59
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:41,280
don't want to leave the house.

60
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:43,000
I don't want to leave this place.

61
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:45,240
I feel the same.

62
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:48,080
It feels so beautiful.

63
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:57,960
We're here.

64
00:04:57,960 --> 00:04:59,080
Let's go.

65
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,480
Let's look around first.

66
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:03,240
Let's see if we can go down there.

67
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:04,600
Okay.

68
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:10,000
It looks so beautiful from here.

69
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:10,920
Yeah.

70
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:17,640
Look at the crab.

71
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:19,240
Whose foot is that huge?

72
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:21,840
Is it yours?

73
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:22,960
My foot isn't that big.

74
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,200
Do you want to walk barefoot?

75
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:28,360
I'll just go barefoot.

76
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,640
Then I'll go barefoot too.

77
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:32,480
Be careful with the path.

78
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:33,520
Careful.

79
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:43,800
Walking barefoot
on the sand feels amazing.

80
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:44,800
It's amazing.

81
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:45,340
Yeah.

82
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:51,740
Careful, don't step on it.

83
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:52,300
(Concerned)

84
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:53,640
Alright.

85
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:54,480
Walk on my side.

86
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,480
Okay.

87
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,120
Look at the stars here.

88
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:06,040
I can't see clearly.

89
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:08,480
Here, this area.

90
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,040
You can do this.

91
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:10,440
Put your hands like this.

92
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,520
Then look through the gap.

93
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,480
There are so many stars.

94
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:15,240
Can you see them?

95
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,360
I can.

96
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:19,520
Does it work?

97
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:20,480
It does.

98
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,560
It's the pinhole camera effect.

99
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:26,240
Physics is pretty cool.

100
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,200
The pinhole effect.

101
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:28,880
Such a science guy.

102
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,760
There's a light shining at me.

103
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:32,480
It's pretty good.

104
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:34,740
(Trying to see clearly)

105
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:36,740
(Notices)

106
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:39,420
(Moves aside)

107
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:42,300
(Blocks the light)

108
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:44,240
This works.

109
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:49,800
A sky full of stars.

110
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,080
So beautiful.

111
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:56,400
Without light pollution,

112
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,680
you can finally see the Milky Way.

113
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:58,360
Yeah.

114
00:06:58,820 --> 00:07:02,260
(Staring)

115
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:09,000
Feel it.

116
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:10,260
(Blocks)

117
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:10,960
It's really nice.

118
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:12,880
Right?

119
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:14,360
There are so many!

120
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,200
After she blocked the light for me,

121
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:20,200
my night suddenly lit up.

122
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,400
It was filled with stars.

123
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:23,440
At that moment, I felt

124
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:24,400
really touched.

125
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:25,440
Yeah.

126
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,240
I'm really happy.

127
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:29,840
Especially because there
were so many stars. It was so beautiful.

128
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,580
It felt like such a pleasant surprise.

129
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:33,460
(Unexpected surprise)

130
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:40,410
Oh my gosh.

131
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:45,040
It looks so pretty.

132
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,400
Where else is there...

133
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:51,860
(Holds)

134
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,520
Be careful.

135
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:56,960
Let's not go any further in.

136
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:57,990
Yeah.

137
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:01,060
(Pulls)

138
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:03,760
Are you okay?

139
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:04,360
I'm fine.

140
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:05,560
Those big waves...

141
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:07,450
Let's go.

142
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:12,040
Happy.

143
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:13,340
Happy.

144
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:14,440
(Happy)

145
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:16,520
Mostly, I'm happy
just walking around with you.

146
00:08:16,520 --> 00:08:17,200
Really?

147
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:18,120
Yeah.

148
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:20,840
Maybe the special thing isn't the beach.

149
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:21,860
(The special thing isn't the beach)

150
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:24,160
It's you.

151
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:28,880
Let's go back up.

152
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:29,680
Okay.

153
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:35,720
This is so romantic.

154
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,240
Yeah.

155
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:41,680
This is so romantic.

156
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:43,600
I actually wish we
could do this every day.

157
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,520
Every day!

158
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:46,080
But then I think
about how many people are still here.

159
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:46,800
Yeah.

160
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,600
Such a shame.

161
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:49,840
We can only do it once.

162
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,000
Each person only gets one chance.

163
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:51,880
No repeats.

164
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:52,840
Right.

165
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,240
But you were the first one to write it.

166
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:56,400
Yeah.

167
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,120
That was really brave.

168
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,400
It wasn't bravery.

169
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:02,060
It was carefully planned.

170
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:11,040
Sit.

171
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:13,880
Have some tea.

172
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:14,680
This one's yours.

173
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:15,760
Drink this one.

174
00:09:16,260 --> 00:09:17,380
(Personal flavor)

175
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:18,880
Okay.

176
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:20,280
I'll have some white tea.

177
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:21,200
Okay.

178
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:25,920
Let's talk.

179
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,640
First...

180
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:32,480
Is there anything you want to ask me?

181
00:09:35,340 --> 00:09:36,660
(Fidgets)

182
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:37,880
What kind of person do you think

183
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:38,800
would make starting a relationship

184
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:40,440
less likely to cause regrets?

185
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:42,440
Here we go.

186
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:43,480
Good question.

187
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,160
I think at this stage of life...

188
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:51,840
I'm already in my twenties.

189
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:54,280
I think at least our

190
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,720
general direction in life should match.

191
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:59,040
And when it comes to values,

192
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:00,720
they should overlap a lot.

193
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,160
Interests and hobbies
aren't that important.

194
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:02,520
The rest

195
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:03,280
can be

196
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:04,440
worked out.

197
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:06,840
But the bigger direction
needs to be the same.

198
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,480
Because I need

199
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,520
to think about the future.

200
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,760
Would you want a long-term relationship?

201
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:18,120
I would.

202
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:19,880
Otherwise, why would I be here?

203
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,960
Also, I really hope that

204
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:27,400
when it comes to our careers,

205
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,240
we don't necessarily need to overlap.

206
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:28,960
But...

207
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:31,160
we both need to know for sure

208
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:33,040
that the other person
is part of our future.

209
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:34,360
(Both knowing the other person
is part of their future)

210
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:36,720
We can each work hard

211
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:37,440
in our own fields,

212
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:38,640
or work hard together

213
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:39,160
in the same field.

214
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:42,120
But we should still feel
like we're on the same journey.

215
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,440
Both people should
be positive and motivated.

216
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:48,360
Even if they're in different fields.

217
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:48,880
Yeah.

218
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:51,220
(Nods)

219
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:52,800
And I think

220
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,440
the way I feel happiness

221
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:56,880
is my feelings come before my thoughts.

222
00:10:58,360 --> 00:10:59,840
Whether you're living in the moment

223
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:01,160
or looking for long-term stability,

224
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:02,880
you should at least be happy right now.

225
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:03,240
So...

226
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:03,880
Exactly.

227
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:05,120
If you're already hesitating now,

228
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:06,920
hesitating about the relationship itself,

229
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:09,160
then that relationship isn't worth it.

230
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:10,240
Exactly.

231
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:21,760
Are you going
to graduate school in September?

232
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:27,880
If I get an offer

233
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:28,640
from Imperial College London,

234
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:29,960
I'll go study there.

235
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:34,960
If I don't get

236
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:35,760
the offer,

237
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:38,720
and I get the offer
from University College London,

238
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:39,760
I might...

239
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:41,440
most likely

240
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:43,640
defer it until next year.

241
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,560
So if you ask me now,

242
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:49,680
I can't give you

243
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:50,470
an exact answer.

244
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:52,560
Because I haven't received my offer yet.

245
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:53,520
That's very honest.

246
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:54,840
Yeah.

247
00:11:58,380 --> 00:12:00,460
(Paying attention)

248
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,040
What do you think?

249
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:04,080
How do you feel
about handling it this way?

250
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:12,360
For example, if you go
study abroad for your master's,

251
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:13,720
what if

252
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:15,960
the other person feels insecure?

253
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:21,380
In a long-distance relationship like this,

254
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:22,320
I'd be willing to keep them updated.

255
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:22,760
I think that's

256
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:23,360
the basic thing to do.

257
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:25,320
For example, when we're

258
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:26,120
in different time zones,

259
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:26,760
when you're sleeping,

260
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,440
I'll tell you things like,

261
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:29,000
I'm going out for dinner,

262
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,440
who I'm having dinner with.

263
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:32,160
I'll send photos and things like that.

264
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:35,060
(Nods)

265
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:37,760
As for the reality of it,

266
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:39,360
all I can do is make plans.

267
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,760
I can't completely remove it.

268
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,080
If it exists, it exists.

269
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:43,120
Exactly.

270
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:45,320
I'd rather work with my partner

271
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,360
to overcome it.

272
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:49,000
Because I think when two people
are attracted to each other,

273
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,440
they should have confidence

274
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,680
in each other and themselves.

275
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:53,120
That's how a relationship works.

276
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:54,520
Exactly.

277
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:06,550
Do you know what you're

278
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:09,920
looking for in a relationship right now?

279
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:11,880
I'm just curious
if you know what you're looking for.

280
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:23,560
I think you have

281
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,480
a really great quality.

282
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,040
You're very determined.

283
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:28,880
That really touched me.

284
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:34,060
(That really touched me)

285
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:39,920
What do you think...

286
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,960
Emotionally, it's good.

287
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,040
What does good mean?

288
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:48,920
Positive.

289
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:50,170
What does positive mean?

290
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:52,400
Positive.

291
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:53,720
What does positive mean?

292
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:54,720
Optimistic.

293
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:55,480
Toward who?

294
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:56,210
Toward you.

295
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:00,840
How positive is it?

296
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:02,440
